<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>booba — Bubble Tea in the browser</title>
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ .Base }}/_assets/booba.png">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ .Base }}/style.css">
</head>
<body class="layout">
<button class="menu-button" aria-label="Toggle navigation">☰</button>
<div class="sidebar-overlay"></div>
{{ template "sidebar" . }}
<main class="main">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>booba</h1>
    <p class="hero-tagline">Bubble Tea terminal apps, in a web browser.</p>
    <p>
      <code>go-booba</code> puts <a href="https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea">Bubble Tea</a>
      programs in the browser on a <a href="https://github.com/coder/ghostty-web">Ghostty</a>-powered terminal.
      Compile a program to WebAssembly and run it with no server, or serve a program over
      WebSocket or WebTransport from a machine that has it. The demos here are the first kind:
      everything you see runs in this page.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/go-booba">View on GitHub</a>
      <a class="cta cta-secondary" href="https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/NimbleMarkets/go-booba">godoc</a>
      <a class="cta cta-secondary" href="https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/go-booba-example">Starter template</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    {{- range .Manifest.Groups }}
    <h2>{{ .Title }}</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      {{- range .Demos }}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ $.Base }}/demos/{{ .Name }}/">
          <strong>{{ .Title }}</strong>
          <span>{{ .BlurbHTML }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {{- end }}
    </ul>
    {{- end }}
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Serving a program</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages can only host static files, so the other half of booba is not on this site.
      The <code>serve</code> package runs a Bubble Tea program, or any command in a PTY, behind an
      HTTP server and bridges browser clients over WebSocket or WebTransport with the same terminal
      front end used here. The <code>booba</code> command does it for any local program:
    </p>
    <pre><code>booba --listen 127.0.0.1:8080 -- htop</code></pre>
    <p>
      See the <a href="https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/go-booba#web-frontend-for-bubbletea-based-service">README</a>
      for the server API and middleware, and
      <a href="https://github.com/NimbleMarkets/go-booba/blob/main/docs/TERMINAL_ACTIONS.md">Terminal Actions</a>
      for the experiment behind the touch-controls demo.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
{{ template "menu-script" . }}
</body>
</html>
